    "result": "Perfect! All 28 tests pass. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\nI fixed two failing tests in the frai-core test suite:\n\n### 1. **governance.test.js** - Missing named export for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`\n**File**: `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`\n\n**Issue**: The test imported `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export.\n\n**Fix**: Added `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` as named exports alongside the default export.\n\n### 2. **eval/index.test.js** - Toxicity metric score incorrect\n**File**: `packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`\n\n**Issue**: The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving `references` as the second parameter but treating it as `bannedTerms`. This caused it to incorrectly flag outputs as toxic when they contained reference text.\n\n**Fix**: Simplified the `toxicityMetric` function signature to only accept `outputs` as a parameter and always use `defaultBannedTerms`. This aligns with how the function is called in the evaluation pipeline.\n\n## Test Results\n\n```\n\u2713 All 8 test files passing\n\u2713 All 28 tests passing\n```\n\nCommands run:\n- `pnpm --filter frai-core test` \u2705 28 passed\n- `pnpm --filter frai-core build` \u2705 Success",
